# Binary Tree Inorder Traversal (Recursive)

## Problem

Return the inorder traversal of a binary tree.

Traversal Order

Left

↓

Root

↓

Right

---

## Algorithm

1. If root is NULL, return.
2. Traverse the left subtree.
3. Visit the current node.
4. Traverse the right subtree.

---

## Dry Run

Tree

        1
      /   \
     2     3
    / \   / \
   4   5 6   7

Traversal

4 → 2 → 5 → 1 → 6 → 3 → 7

Output

4 2 5 1 6 3 7

---

## Time Complexity

O(n)

Every node is visited exactly once.

---

## Space Complexity

O(h)

h = Height of the tree

Worst Case: O(n)

Balanced Tree: O(log n)

---

## Important Points

✅ Base Case

```cpp
if(root == NULL)
    return;
```

✅ Pass vector by reference

```cpp
vector<int>& ans
```

No extra copy is created.

✅ Inorder means

Left

↓

Root

↓

Right

---

## Pattern

```cpp
inorder(left);

Visit Root;

inorder(right);
```

---

## Difference

Preorder

Root → Left → Right

Inorder

Left → Root → Right

Postorder

Left → Right → Root